---
// Caution tape over a planned project's slate (PRD §5.3): the "still
// building this" signal, in place of any dimming — the frame itself stays
// at full strength. Yellow-and-black diagonal bands, construction-site
// tape, in the one hazard colour (--hazard). Decorative: no text on it,
// hidden from assistive tech (the slate says "In production" in real text).
//
// Increment 34: an X of two strips, each the full diagonal, corner to
// corner, like a door taped shut — in place of increment 33's X of two
// short strips and a third beside it, and increment 30's single band
// across the top. Rendered by PlannedCard.astro over the slate, so the X
// spans the picture area's diagonals at any size.
---

<div class="tape" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="strip down"></div>
  <div class="strip up"></div>
</div>

<style>
  /* The layer is the slate's box grown by the tape's overhang (still
     inside the frame's 0.75rem side margin, so nothing leaves the frame at
     320px). A size container, so each strip can be as long as a share of
     its diagonal and turned to it: hypot() and atan2() of the container's
     own width and height. */
  .tape {
    position: absolute;
    inset: -0.375rem;
    z-index: 1;
    container-type: size;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* Centred on the layer, then turned onto a diagonal. Exactly the
     diagonal's length, so each strip's centre line ends in a corner of the
     layer (the tape's overhang past the slate's corner) and its square ends
     lap just over the edge, the way tape wraps a board. The stops are
     softened by a pixel so the bands render smooth, not stair-stepped. */
  .strip {
    --diag: hypot(100cqw, 100cqh);
    --tilt: atan2(100cqh, 100cqw);
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    width: var(--diag);
    /* In proportion to the slate, so a phone's small one is not buried:
       ~10px at 320, capped at 18px from about 768. */
    height: clamp(0.625rem, 6.5cqh, 1.125rem);
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(
      -45deg,
      var(--hazard) 0 10.5px,
      var(--monitor-bg) 11.5px 21.5px,
      var(--hazard) 22.5px 22.5px
    );
    box-shadow: 0 2px 6px var(--shadow);
    translate: -50% -50%;
  }

  /* "\" top-left to bottom-right, "/" bottom-left to top-right. */
  .down {
    rotate: var(--tilt);
  }

  .up {
    rotate: calc(-1 * var(--tilt));
  }
</style>
